          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="synthesis">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">05 — Synthesis & Discussion</div>
    <h2 class="title reveal">Turning evidence into a design direction.</h2>
    <p class="lead reveal">Observation, interview and questionnaire findings were compared to identify four recurring themes.</p>

    <div class="synthesis">
      <article class="theme reveal"><h3>Comfort, Resting & Accessibility</h3><p>Existing facilities do not fully provide comfortable, accessible and attractive spaces for visitors to rest and move through long or steep routes.</p></article>
      <article class="theme reveal"><h3>Interactive Learning & Recreation</h3><p>Visitors need facilities that combine recreation, information and engaging nature learning.</p></article>
      <article class="theme reveal"><h3>Social Interaction & Community Engagement</h3><p>The product should support group use, social activities and a simple way to contribute ideas.</p></article>
      <article class="theme reveal"><h3>Sustainability & Maintenance</h3><p>Future facilities should use durable, eco-friendly and easy-maintenance materials suited to the park environment.</p></article>
    </div>

    <div class="priority">
      <div class="priority-row reveal"><span class="priority-label high">High Priority</span><strong>Limited comfort and resting facilities</strong><span>Old, empty or poorly maintained shelters and only moderate user satisfaction.</span></div>
      <div class="priority-row reveal"><span class="priority-label high">High Priority</span><strong>Limited accessibility and mobility support</strong><span>Steep routes, visitor fatigue, limited tram seating and waiting time.</span></div>
      <div class="priority-row reveal"><span class="priority-label mhigh">Medium–High</span><strong>Limited interactive learning and recreation</strong><span>Static information and strong interest in new interactive products.</span></div>
      <div class="priority-row reveal"><span class="priority-label mhigh">Medium–High</span><strong>Poor maintenance and unattractive facilities</strong><span>Observed damage and requests for repaired, improved facilities.</span></div>
      <div class="priority-row reveal"><span class="priority-label medium">Medium</span><strong>Sustainability and durability</strong><span>Preference for durable products and eco-friendly materials.</span></div>
      <div class="priority-row reveal"><span class="priority-label low">Low–Medium</span><strong>Limited feedback systems</strong><span>Interest exists, but time, complexity and limited platforms create barriers.</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="trace-table reveal">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Research Finding</th><th>Design Requirement</th><th>Proposed Feature</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Visitor fatigue</td><td>Comfortable resting support</td><td>Shaded ergonomic seating</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Steep and long routes</td><td>Mobility and stopping support</td><td>Rest hub near walking and cycling routes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Limited tram seating</td><td>Waiting support</td><td>Integrated waiting area</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Static information boards</td><td>Improve interaction</td><td>Interactive nature-learning panel</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Group visits</td><td>Support social use</td><td>Shared and flexible seating</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Limited feedback platform</td><td>Simple participation</td><td>QR community feedback</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Poor maintenance</td><td>Reduce maintenance burden</td><td>Durable modular construction</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sustainable product preference</td><td>Reduce environmental impact</td><td>Eco-friendly and repairable materials</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Need for visitor information</td><td>Improve park understanding</td><td>Map, signage and attraction information</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section soft" id="concept">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">06 — Concept Design</div>
    <h2 class="title reveal">Three directions. One final solution.</h2>
    <p class="lead reveal">The concepts were developed from the research criteria rather than from form exploration alone.</p>

    <div class="concepts">
      <article class="concept reveal">
        <div class="concept-top"><span>Concept 01</span><strong>32</strong></div>
        <h3>Eco-Mobility Rest Hub</h3>
        <p><strong>Main issue:</strong> comfort, resting, accessibility and mobility.</p>
        <ul><li>Shaded ergonomic seating</li><li>Bicycle and scooter parking</li><li>Accessible circulation</li><li>Waiting and resting space</li><li>Visitor information</li><li>Sustainable construction</li></ul>
        <p><strong>Strength:</strong> strongest response to the highest-priority problems.</p>
        <p><strong>Weakness:</strong> limited interactive learning and feedback.</p>
        <div class="badge">Selected Main Direction</div>
      </article>

      <article class="concept reveal">
        <div class="concept-top"><span>Concept 02</span><strong>25</strong></div>
        <h3>Interactive Nature Discovery Station</h3>
        <p><strong>Main issue:</strong> passive information and limited interactive learning.</p>
        <ul><li>Nature-learning panel</li><li>QR educational content</li><li>Park map and route information</li><li>Flora and fauna information</li><li>Tactile elements</li><li>Small shaded seating</li></ul>
        <p><strong>Strength:</strong> strongest nature-learning direction.</p>
        <p><strong>Weakness:</strong> limited mobility and long-distance rest support.</p>
        <div class="badge">Nature-Learning Feature Selected</div>
      </article>

      <article class="concept reveal">
        <div class="concept-top"><span>Concept 03</span><strong>27</strong></div>
        <h3>Modular Community Activity Pavilion</h3>
        <p><strong>Main issue:</strong> social interaction, flexible use and participation.</p>
        <ul><li>Modular seating</li><li>Shared activity table</li><li>Flexible furniture</li><li>Community notice panel</li><li>Group discussion space</li><li>QR suggestion system</li></ul>
        <p><strong>Strength:</strong> strongest community-engagement direction.</p>
        <p><strong>Weakness:</strong> greater space and maintenance complexity.</p>
        <div class="badge">Participation Feature Selected</div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3 class="subtitle reveal" style="margin-top:72px">Concept Evaluation Method</h3>
    <p class="lead reveal">The researcher used a five-point scale. Scores were based on research findings, user needs, design criteria, sustainability and feasibility. Each criterion received equal importance.</p>

    <div class="rubric">
      <div class="reveal"><strong>1</strong><span>Very weak response</span></div>
      <div class="reveal"><strong>2</strong><span>Weak response</span></div>
      <div class="reveal"><strong>3</strong><span>Moderate response</span></div>
      <div class="reveal"><strong>4</strong><span>Good response</span></div>
      <div class="reveal"><strong>5</strong><span>Very strong response</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="matrix reveal">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Evaluation Criteria</th><th>Concept 1</th><th>Concept 2</th><th>Concept 3</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Comfort and resting</td><td class="score best">5</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">4</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Accessibility and mobility</td><td class="score best">5</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Interactive learning</td><td class="score">4</td><td class="score best">5</td><td class="score">4</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Community engagement</td><td class="score">4</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score best">5</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sustainability</td><td class="score best">5</td><td class="score">4</td><td class="score">4</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Maintenance feasibility</td><td class="score best">4</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Overall research relevance</td><td class="score best">5</td><td class="score">4</td><td class="score">4</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td class="score best"><strong>32</strong></td><td class="score"><strong>25</strong></td><td class="score"><strong>27</strong></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="calc reveal">Calculation: Concept 1 = 5 + 5 + 4 + 4 + 5 + 4 + 5 = 32 &nbsp; | &nbsp; Concept 2 = 25 &nbsp; | &nbsp; Concept 3 = 27</div>

    <div class="score-why">
      <details class="reveal"><summary>Why Concept 1 scored highest in comfort, accessibility and relevance</summary><p>Its main functions directly respond to visitor fatigue, steep routes, cycling, tram waiting, accessible movement and sustainable rest support. These were the highest-priority research problems.</p></details>
      <details class="reveal"><summary>Why Concept 2 scored highest in interactive learning</summary><p>Nature education, flora and fauna information, tactile elements and QR educational content are the central functions of the concept.</p></details>
      <details class="reveal"><summary>Why Concept 3 scored highest in community engagement</summary><p>Its modular group seating, shared activity table, discussion space, notice panel and QR suggestion system directly support participation and social use.</p></details>
      <details class="reveal"><summary>Why maintenance scores were not 5</summary><p>All concepts contain outdoor structures and components requiring inspection. Concepts 2 and 3 include more learning or movable activity elements, which may increase maintenance complexity.</p></details>
    </div>

    <div class="selection reveal">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Final Selection</div><h3>Eco-Interactive Mobility Rest Hub</h3></div>
      <p>Concept 1 was selected because it achieved the highest total and responded most strongly to comfort, resting, accessibility and mobility. Selected strengths from Concepts 2 and 3 were integrated to improve nature learning, visitor information and community participation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="merge">
      <article class="merge-card reveal"><b>Concept 1</b><h4>Main Product Structure</h4><p>Rest hub, ergonomic seating, accessible circulation and mobility support.</p></article>
      <article class="merge-card reveal"><b>Concept 2</b><h4>Learning Feature</h4><p>Interactive nature-learning and visitor-information panel.</p></article>
      <article class="merge-card reveal"><b>Concept 3</b><h4>Participation Feature</h4><p>QR community feedback and simple digital suggestion platform.</p></article>
    </div>

    <div class="final-grid">
      <figure class="final-visual reveal"><img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="Eco-Interactive Mobility Rest Hub concept board"></figure>
      <div class="final-copy reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow">Final Concept Features</div>
        <h3>Rest. Move. Learn. Participate.</h3>
        <div class="features">
          <div class="feature"><b>01</b><div><h4>Shaded Ergonomic Seating</h4><p>Supports comfort during walking, cycling and waiting.</p></div></div>
          <div class="feature"><b>02</b><div><h4>Mobility Rest Point</h4><p>A strategic stopping point along long and steep routes.</p></div></div>
          <div class="feature"><b>03</b><div><h4>Integrated Waiting Area</h4><p>Provides additional support for tram users.</p></div></div>
          <div class="feature"><b>04</b><div><h4>Nature-Learning Panel</h4><p>Creates a more engaging environmental learning experience.</p></div></div>
          <div class="feature"><b>05</b><div><h4>Shared Seating</h4><p>Supports friends, families and group interaction.</p></div></div>
          <div class="feature"><b>06</b><div><h4>QR Community Feedback</h4><p>Allows visitors to share ideas through a simple digital channel.</p></div></div>
          <div class="feature"><b>07</b><div><h4>Modular Construction</h4><p>Supports easier maintenance and replacement.</p></div></div>
          <div class="feature"><b>08</b><div><h4>Eco-Friendly Materials</h4><p>Reduces environmental impact and supports long-term durability.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="subtitle reveal" style="margin-top:72px">Concept UX & Usage Scenario</h3>
    <div class="scenario-grid">
      <article class="scenario reveal"><b>Before Usage</b><h4>Fatigue Appears</h4><p>The visitor becomes tired while walking or cycling along a long and steep route.</p></article>
      <article class="scenario reveal"><b>Approach</b><h4>Rest Hub Identified</h4><p>The visitor sees the shaded hub, parks the bicycle or scooter and enters through accessible circulation.</p></article>
      <article class="scenario reveal"><b>During Usage</b><h4>Rest, Learn & Socialise</h4><p>The visitor rests, checks route information, reads nature content and interacts with others.</p></article>
      <article class="scenario reveal"><b>After Usage</b><h4>Feedback & Continue</h4><p>The visitor scans the QR code, shares feedback and continues the park journey more comfortably.</p></article>
    </div>
    <figure class="story reveal"><img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="Usage scenario storyboard"></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section dark" id="outcome">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">07 — Expected Outcome & Conclusion</div>
    <h2 class="title reveal">A complete research-to-design response.</h2>
    <p class="lead reveal">The Eco-Interactive Mobility Rest Hub is expected to improve visitor comfort, accessibility and mobility while encouraging nature learning, social interaction, environmental awareness and simple community participation.</p>

    <div class="achievement">
      <article class="achieve reveal"><span>Achieved</span><h3>Research Objective 1</h3><p>Online platforms, questionnaires and mobile-based participation were identified as suitable methods.</p></article>
      <article class="achieve reveal"><span>Achieved within scope</span><h3>Research Objective 2</h3><p>Selected facilities were analysed and issues involving comfort, accessibility, interaction, maintenance and sustainability were identified.</p></article>
      <article class="achieve reveal"><span>Achieved within scope</span><h3>Research Objective 3</h3><p>Three concepts were produced, evaluated and developed into one final concept with a usage scenario.</p></article>
    </div>

    <div class="two" style="margin-top:62px">
      <div class="reveal"><h3 class="subtitle">Conclusion</h3></div>
      <p class="lead reveal">This study successfully identified suitable participatory design methods, analysed selected facilities at TBNSA and translated the findings into an environmentally responsible community product concept. The final concept responds to visitor comfort, resting, accessibility and mobility needs while integrating nature learning, visitor information and digital community participation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

